.TH PS 1
.SH NAME
ps \- the running programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ps
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ps
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It prints one line per process, from the kernel's list
.RB ( sys_tasks (2)):
.TP
.B PID PPID UID
its number, its parent's (0: started by the kernel), its user's
.TP
.B CPU
where its first thread runs (or last ran)
.TP
.B THR
its number of threads
.TP
.B STATE
its most active thread's:
.B run
or
.B ready
(running or about to),
.B send
and
.B reply
(waiting for a server's answer),
.B recv
(a server waiting for messages),
.B lookup
(waiting for a server to exist),
.BR sleep ,
.B wait
(for a child),
.B dead
.TP
.B MEM
the memory it uses, KiB
.TP
.B NAME
its program's name
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kill (1),
.BR mem (1),
.BR svc (8)
